# Task 10 — KPI Stat Cards

**Category:** Data Display
**Difficulty:** above-average
**Style school:** Material Design 3

## The problem

A grid of stat cards (number + trend indicator) that stays visually
consistent across a dashboard, no matter how many stats are shown.

## Constraints

- Every card must render from the same reusable component with different
  inputs — no copy-pasted card markup per stat.

## Key implementation decisions

- Introduced the project's first shared component: `shared/ui/stat-card`.
  It exposes `label`, `value`, `trend`, and `trendLabel` as signal-based
  inputs (`input()` / `input.required()`), matching the same reactive style
  used throughout the project (signals/computed) instead of the older
  `@Input()` decorator.
- `trend` defaults to `'flat'` and drives conditional styling (`up` = brand
  color with an up arrow, `down` = muted color with a down arrow) purely via
  class bindings — no separate component variant needed per trend direction.
- The trend line is wrapped in `@if (trendLabel())` so a future card with no
  trend data at all doesn't render an empty, awkwardly spaced line.

